A||||7||lennyb4||Trunk Release..||||5||
Z||000000||lennyb4||05-19-2000||11:40 AM||||I thought i heard someone say that the 87 fiero's all came with the necessary trunk release wiring and actuators all ready installed (just missing the switch?). Is this true? If so does anyone know where i can get a switch and panel from?<P>TIA....<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||lennyb4||05-19-2000||01:56 PM||||Hello????? Anybody out there???? Just kiddin, i just dont want this thread to get booted down before i can get an answer.||||reg||12
Z||000002||fiero56||05-19-2000||02:13 PM||||Guess I will take a swing at this one. Yes, all Fieros are prewired for remote trunk release AND rear defrost. Take off the rear instrument clutster cover and just behind the dash opening you will see the plugs sitting there. I have no idea where to hook it up in back though. You will also need relay, decklid wiring, and also a release solonoid.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 05-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||DRH||05-19-2000||02:16 PM||||The following applies to my 88 Formula. I believe an 87 will be the same. They come with MOST of the wiring. <P>You need:<BR>- the switch<BR>- the actuator (bolts to latch)<BR>- the wire harness that runs thru the decklid<BR>- a relay (mounts under dash on right side of steering column)<P>The rest of the wiring, including connectors, should be there. To replace the harness that runs thru the decklid... attach a piece of wire or twine to the old harness to use to fish the new harness back thru.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||05-19-2000||02:32 PM||||go to the cave link at the bottom of this page.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DRH||05-19-2000||02:41 PM||||MUCH more detailed info than mine.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>Good job Ogre... Looks really nice and very thorough!!!<P>||||reg||14
Z||000006||lennyb4||05-19-2000||02:43 PM||||Hey thanks guys. I was pretty sure that they came pre-wired for this. And Orge.. cant tell you enough how much your instructions are going to help, didnt think it would be that easy..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000007||theogre||05-20-2000||05:35 PM||||When I first saw how the parts were done, I was like,,,, It can't be this easy. It's a GM. It can't be this easy. <P>but it is. it almost installs itself. It's almost imposible to get wrong.<P>Do keep in mind that the default setup basicly leaves the trunk unlocked to anyone that can reach the switch. Read the security issues carefully. (I altered mine so it will only open if the key is in the run position.)<P>This is another article that has changes coming. some of the posible options to improve security listed in the main article have proven invalid or impractical. Don't use that main article's recomendations. The second article about security is correct and tested. use that one.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 05-20-2000).]||||reg||1
